# Totem

## Pre-Publication Clean-Slate Authority

Policy ID: `pre-publication-clean-slate-v1`.

- Treat this site and all systems that consume it as pre-publication dogfood, even when a development URL is publicly reachable.
- Until the human explicitly removes this authority, choose the best current architecture. Full rewrites and clean contract replacements are authorized when they improve correctness, security, maintainability, performance, accessibility, or product quality.
- Verify replacements end to end, migrate every dogfood caller to one current contract, remove superseded implementation in the same completed change, and finish tests, documentation, security review, and cleanup before deployment.
- Preserve immutable receipts and historical failure evidence as audit truth, never as a promise to support obsolete product behavior.

## Documentation Integrity Authority

- Treat the retained redirect, destination, retirement notice, and bounded historical evidence as this site's documentation product. Keep each statement and destination synchronized with the current TinyRustLM developer portal.
- Clearly label historical evidence by date and scope. Never present retired Runtime.MiRust.com behavior as a current contract, current implementation, current deployment, or compatibility promise.
- Verify redirect behavior, canonical destination, status code, HTTPS behavior, accessible fallback text, historical-evidence links, and public readback after every affected publication.
- Block publication when destination guidance or historical labels are stale, broken, contradictory, unverified, or inconsistent with TinyRustLM.MiRust.com and the authoritative release record.
- Remove superseded user guidance after its replacement is verified. Preserve immutable historical receipts separately; historical evidence is not legacy product support.
